+### Requirement: POC-REQ-014 — Every work item's governing intent renders as a counted Unknown
+
+Group: Work-item observation. Form: **invariant**.
+
+**Required behavior.** Every served work item SHALL carry a governing-intent
+field (`governedBy`) whose value is `Unknown` with the primary reason
+`source-uncaptured-or-unreachable` and that reason's RFC2-24 resolution
+route. Both channels SHALL serve how many served items carry that Unknown,
+over the served item set. Trajectory SHALL mark each such item, show the
+count, state beside it that an item is resolved by supplying its warrant, and
+let a reader narrow the board to those items. No served item's `governedBy`
+SHALL name an identifier taken from its title. Every such item SHALL render
+with its Unknown marker, never as warranted, green or complete, and no
+Unknown marker SHALL replace or hide an orphaned-work Contradiction where one
+is rendered.
+
+- **Scope.** every served work item in the machine answer and on Trajectory.
+  This requirement admits no work-item column and no other input: the
+  projection stays as POC-REQ-010 to POC-REQ-013 bound it. It defines no
+  edge. An edge to a warrant, and the input that would carry one, need a
+  further amendment.
+
+- **Case (sweep + counterexample schema)**: a checker enumerates every served
+  work item from the machine answer — the denominator is the complete served
+  item set (POC-REQ-011) — and reads each item's `governedBy`. Separately,
+  the checker supplies a fixture work-item database (or an injected work-item
+  read) holding one item whose title names a requirement identifier, for
+  example "Implement POC-REQ-010", and observes that item.
+- **Observable**: each item's `governedBy` value, reason and route; the served
+  Unknown count and item count on both channels; on Trajectory, each item's
+  Unknown marker, the count, the resolution sentence beside it, and the list
+  of items the board shows once narrowed.
+- **Oracle**: every enumerated item's `governedBy` is `Unknown` with the
+  reason `source-uncaptured-or-unreachable` and the route RFC2-24 gives that
+  reason; the served Unknown count equals the enumerated item count, and the
+  two channels serve the same count; Trajectory's narrowed board lists exactly
+  the enumerated items; and the fixture item's `governedBy` is that same
+  Unknown, naming no identifier. Equality and set membership decide.
+- **Oracle independence**: the denominator is the checker's own enumeration
+  of served items, not the served count; the reason and its route are read
+  from RFC2-24; the fixture title is the checker's own.
+- **Falsifier**: a served item with no `governedBy`; a `governedBy` holding
+  anything other than that Unknown, including an identifier from its title;
+  any other reason, or a route that is not RFC2-24's route for this reason;
+  a count that does not equal the enumeration or differs between the
+  channels; no resolution sentence; a narrowed board that drops or adds an
+  item; or an item rendered as warranted, green or complete.
+
+#### Scenario: Every item's governing intent is Unknown
+
+- **WHEN** the machine answer serves N work items
+- **THEN** both channels serve N of N with `governedBy` Unknown for the
+  reason `source-uncaptured-or-unreachable` and its route, and Trajectory
+  marks all N, says each is resolved by supplying its warrant, and lets a
+  reader narrow the board to them
+
+#### Scenario: A title names a requirement
+
+- **WHEN** a served item's title reads "Implement POC-REQ-010"
+- **THEN** that item's `governedBy` is the same Unknown, and nothing served
+  for it names POC-REQ-010 as its governing intent
+
+```yaml
+warrants:
+  primary: VIS-2
+  doctrine: [VIS-1, VIS-2, VIS-6]
+  contracts: [RFC2-24, RFC4-15, RFC8-22, RFC8-23, RFC8-24]
+  policies: []
+  decisions: []
+  topology: []
+  parent_requirements: []
+```
+
